# Project Skills

The canonical, tool-neutral home for this repo's own agent skills — committed to
source control. Claude Code discovers this directory through the `.claude/skills`
symlink that points here; other harnesses are directed here by the pointer in
`AGENTS.md`.

## Adding a skill

One skill per directory: `<skill-name>/SKILL.md` (kebab-case). The file follows
the open agent-skills format — YAML frontmatter, then an imperative body:

```yaml
---
name: <kebab-case, matches the folder>
description: <one line, written as a trigger — "Use when...">
---
```

`description` is the only thing an agent reads when deciding whether the skill
applies — make it a trigger, not a title. In Claude Code, a skill added here
appears in the next session's available-skills list and is invocable as
`/<skill-name>`.

## Where skills come from

Skills here are the top rung of the harness's self-improvement ladder:
**correction → lesson → rule → skill**. A correction becomes a
`.claude/lessons.md` entry; a recurring lesson graduates into a `CLAUDE.md`
rule; a lesson that describes a whole repeatable workflow — how we run
migrations, how we cut a release — graduates into a skill here. The
`/adlc:add-skill` skill authors them: it gates on skill-sized workflows,
checks for duplicates, and handles the lesson-graduation bookkeeping.
One-line rules do not belong here.

